<title>FRANCE: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>FRANCE GOVERNMENT LIST (970602)</p>
<p>***********************************************************</p>
<p>* 02 Jun 97 - French Prime Minister Alain Juppe resigned  *</p>
<p>*		 and Socialist Lionel Jospin was appointed   *</p>
<p>*		 after final results showed the Socialists   *</p>
<p>*		 and their allies won 273 seats in the 577   *</p>
<p>*		 seat National Assembly and the Communists 38*</p>
<p>*		 after the runoff round in the elections.    *</p>
<p>***********************************************************</p>
<p> President (Inaugurated 17 May 95)..............Jacques CHIRAC</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>Prime Minister..Lionel JOSPIN**</p>
<p>     (Apptd 2 June 97)			    (**See NOTE Above)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING GOVERNMENT (Formed 7 Nov 1995)</p>
<p> Prime Minister (Apptd 17 May 95)............Alain JUPPE (RPR)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture, Fisheries &amp; Food.......Philippe VASSEUR (UDF-PR)</p>
<p>Civil Service, State Reform &amp;</p>
<p>Decentralisation.....DOMINIQUE PERBEN (RPR)</p>
<p> Culture........Philippe DOUSTE-BLAZY (UDF-CDS)</p>
<p> Defence................Charles MILLON (UDF-PR)</p>
<p> Economy &amp; Finance.......Jean ARTHUIS (UDF-CDS)</p>
<p> Education............Francois BAYROU (UDF-CDS)</p>
<p> Environment.........Corinne LEPAGE (non-party)</p>
<p>Equipment, Housing, Transport &amp; Tourism....Bernard PONS (RPR)</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...........Herve DE CHARETTE (UDF-Perspective)</p>
<p>Industry, Post Office &amp;</p>
<p>Telecommunications.....Franck BOROTRA (RPR)</p>
<p> Interior................Jean-Louis DEBRE (RPR)</p>
<p>Justice....Jacques TOUBON (RPR)</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Social Affairs..............Jacques BARROT (UDF-CDS)</p>
<p>Relations with Parliament...Roger ROMANI (RPR)</p>
<p>Small, Medium Business, Commerce &amp;</p>
<p>    Crafts...........Jean-Pierre RAFFARIN (UDF)</p>
<p>Territorial Planning, Urban Affairs &amp;</p>
<p>    Integration........Jean-Claude GAUDIN (UDF)</p>
<p>			- - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS DELEGATE</p>
<p>Delegated to the Economy &amp; Finance Minister,</p>
<p>    Budget &amp; Government Spokesman.......Alain LAMASSOURE (UDF)</p>
<p>Finance &amp; Foreign Trade..Yves GALLAND (UDF)</p>
<p>Delegated to the Equipment, Housing,</p>
<p>Transport &amp; Tourism Minister:</p>
<p>    Housing.........Pierre-Andre PERISSOL (RPR)</p>
<p>Delegated to the Foreign Minister:</p>
<p>    Cooperation..........Jacques GODFRAIN (RPR)</p>
<p>    European Affairs.......Michel BARNIER (RPR)</p>
<p>Delegated to the Industry, Post Office</p>
<p>Telecommunications Minister:</p>
<p>Post Office, Telecommunications &amp;</p>
<p>Space..Francois FILLON (RPR)Z Delegated to the Labour &amp; Social Affairs Minister:</p>
<p>    Employment.........Anne-Marie COUDERC (RPR)</p>
<p>Delegated to the Prime Minister:</p>
<p>    Overseas Territories.........Jean-Jacques DE PERETTI (RPR)</p>
<p>    Veterans Affairs......Pierre PASQUINI (RPR)</p>
<p>    Youth &amp; Sports...............Guy DRUT (RPR)</p>
<p>Delegated to the Territorial Planning Minister,</p>
<p>Urban Affairs &amp; Integration:</p>
<p>    Urban Affairs &amp; Integration..............Eric RAOULT (RPR)</p>
<p>			- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>SECRETARIES OF STATE:</p>
<p>At the Education Ministry:</p>
<p>    Research............Francois d'Aubert (UDF)</p>
<p>At the Equipment, Housing,</p>
<p>Transport &amp; Tourism Ministry:</p>
<p>    Transport......Anne-Marie IDRAC (non-party)</p>
<p>At the Foreign Affairs Ministry:</p>
<p>    Francophone Affairs...............Margie SUDRE (non-party)</p>
<p>At the Labour &amp; Social Affairs Ministry:</p>
<p>    Health and Social Security.............Herve GAYMARD (RPR)</p>
<p>At the Prime Minister's Office:</p>
<p>For Emergency Humanitarian</p>
<p>	 Action.....Xavier EMMANUELLI (non-party)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>RPR - Rally for the Republic</p>
<p>UDF - Union for French Democracy, umbrella group which</p>
<p>	    also includes PR (Republican Party), CDS (Social</p>
<p>	    Democratic Centre), Perspective (Perspective et</p>
<p>	    realites), Radical (Radical Party)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> National Assembly Speaker......Philippe SEGUIN</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor......Jean-Claude TRICHET</p>
